        <ArticleTitle>Early identification of sepsis in the emergency department: a prospective cohort study.</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND">Early recognition of sepsis is critical for improving outcomes.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="METHODS">We enrolled 1,200 adults presenting to the emergency department with suspected infection.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="RESULTS">qSOFA score of 2 or higher had sensitivity of 0.61 and specificity of 0.81 for in-hospital mortality.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS">qSOFA is a useful but imperfect bedside screening tool.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
